questions.question:
Rewrite the following program segment using while instead of for statement.
int f = 1, i;
for (i = 1; i <= 5; i++) {
    f *= i;
    System.out.println(f);
}

questions.solution:
int f = 1, i;
i = 1;
while (i <= 5) {
    f *= i;
    System.out.println(f);
    i++;
}
(Prints 1, 2, 6, 24, 120 on separate lines, same as the for loop.)

